<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Implats half yr shr rises. [CORRECTED 12:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Implats half yr shr rises. [CORRECTED 12:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline to show earnings per share rose, not fell.)</p>
<p>Half yr to December 31 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			 154   vs   149.0</p>
<p>(Corrects 1996 figure to 154 from 134.)</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			 30.0  vs    30.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income		   95.9  vs    92.7 </p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  155.6  vs   132.4 </p>
<p>    Lease, royalties, tax	 10.7  vs    19.7 </p>
<p>Tax effect of spending on</p>
<p>	  future capacity	 59.0    vs    35.2</p>
<p>    Turnover		   1,268.3    vs 1,182.2</p>
<p>    Div payable: April 3	  </p>
<p>    On register: March 7	     </p>
<p>Full name: Impala Platinum Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a concensus</p>
<p>EPS of 120.0 with the range 110.0-155.0 and a dividend of 30.0  </p>
<p>cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
